      "url": "",
      "publishedDate": "2003-04-16T00:00:00.000Z",
      "summary": "On April 16, 2003, NASA's Terra satellite captured a significant dust storm over the Middle East, affecting Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, and southern Iraq. The image shows a series of dust waves, with a lighter outer wave extending over the Persian Gulf and a prominent wave arcing from the bottom left through the center of the image. This event highlights the region's susceptibility to dust storms, which can impact air quality and visibility.",
