    {
      "id": "",
      "title": "NASA Orbiter Camera Team Begins Daily Mars Picture Postings",
      "url": "",
      "publishedDate": "2003-04-15T00:00:00.000Z",
      "author": "Jet Propulsion Laboratory ",
      "summary": "On April 16, 2003, NASA's Mars Global Surveyor camera team continued their initiative of posting daily images of Mars online. The site features a new picture each day, showcasing diverse Martian landscapes, such as frost-covered sand dunes in spring. This effort provides the public with ongoing access to over 123,800 images captured by the spacecraft since its orbit began in September 1997. The initiative aims to enhance public engagement with Mars exploration through accessible, daily visual updates.",
